## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

### Summary

**10 tests analyzed · 9 Critical findings · 1 Medium**

This test suite is a textbook **coverage-touching** class. Every public method on `ProductCatalog` is called (giving you that 95% line coverage), but almost nothing is actually verified. Bugs slip through because these tests will pass no matter what the code returns or does.

---

### 🔴 Critical Findings

#### 1. Systematic Coverage-Touching (class-wide)

All 10 tests follow the same template: call a method, skip the assertion (or use a trivial `IsNotNull`). They walk the entire public API in declaration order. This inflates coverage while verifying zero behavior.

---

#### 2. No Assertion — `AddProduct_Works` (line 17)

```csharp
// CURRENT — proves nothing
_catalog.AddProduct(product);

// FIX
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(retrieved);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved.Price);
```

#### 3. No Assertion — `UpdatePrice_Works` (line 33)

```csharp
// CURRENT — calls UpdatePrice, never checks the new price
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);

// FIX
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated!.Price);
```

#### 4. No Assertion — `RemoveProduct_Works` (line 39)

```csharp
// CURRENT — removes but never verifies removal
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");

// FIX
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
```

#### 5. No Assertion — `GetProductCount_Works` (line 63)

```csharp
// CURRENT — discards the return value entirely
var count = _catalog.GetProductCount();

// FIX
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
var count = _catalog.GetProductCount();
Assert.AreEqual(1, count);
```

#### 6. No Assertion — `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (line 69)

```csharp
// CURRENT — applies 10% discount, never checks prices changed
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);

// FIX — verify the discount math (9.99 * 0.90 = 8.991)
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
Assert.AreEqual(8.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Price);
Assert.AreEqual(17.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-002")!.Price);
```

